# Zetaris rules

Zetaris Lightning 2.4.3.1 runs locally in Docker. JDBC `jdbc:zetaris:lightning@localhost:10000`, driver class `com.zetaris.lightning.jdbc.LightningDriver`, driver JAR from `ZETARIS_JDBC_JAR`. UI http://localhost:3000, API 8888, Spark UI 4040 (the cache truth: its storage tab lists every cached table). Never call port 8889. The driver is shared with another project's cached tables: never CACHE, UNCACHE or read anything outside the objects below.

## Writing SQL

- Lightning SQL only. Not Spark SQL or Hive SQL; never start a local Spark session.
- One statement per call, no trailing semicolon, qualified names (`<database>.<table>`, `cw.<view>`).
- A multi-table `COMPILE USL ... DDL CREATE TABLE ...; CREATE TABLE ...` is ONE statement. Never split it on `;`.
- `CREATE LIGHTNING DATABASE` and `CREATE SCHEMASTORE CONTAINER` do not accept `IF NOT EXISTS` on 2.4.3.1 (parse error `mismatched input 'not'`); rerun scripts with `--skip-exists` instead. `CREATE NAMESPACE IF NOT EXISTS` and `COMPILE USL IF NOT EXISTS` are fine; `lightning.metastore` must exist before `lightning.metastore.crosswalk`.
- `tag` is a reserved word in the Lightning catalog parser: the USL column is `xbrl_tag`. Table-level composite primary keys are accepted.
- `UPDATE USL ... SET [TABLE | COLUMN] DESCRIPTION <text>` takes unquoted text (a quoted string is stored with its quotes); no semicolon or apostrophe in the text.
- Nested JSON is read with `LATERAL VIEW explode(...)` in a SchemaStore view (`CREATE SCHEMASTORE VIEW <v> WITH CONTAINER cw AS SELECT ...`); never select street address fields from SEC submissions.
- Frames `cik` is an integer: join with `LPAD(CAST(cik AS STRING), 10, '0')`. Frames `val` is inferred `double` for some periods and `bigint` for others: `CAST(val AS DOUBLE)` downstream.
- Arithmetic that feeds a USL `double` column must be double from the source (`CAST(... AS DOUBLE)`); a decimal result raises `java.math.BigDecimal is not a valid external type for schema of double` on aggregates over the USL table.
- Degree days are computed in SQL over the cached station views: `Tmean F = ((TMAX + TMIN) / 2.0) / 10.0 * 9.0 / 5.0 + 32`, HDD and CDD with base 65, days with a non-empty `Q_FLAG` on either element dropped, in the same evaluation order as `agent/src/tools/degreeDays.ts`.
- Every read of a filestore (parquet) table costs about 9 s of Zetaris-side source resolution per table per view level, regardless of the cache: ask for all stations of a period in ONE `weather_quarter` call (up to 40 ids, about 19 s), never one call per utility, and never read the USL weather table at question time (about 3 minutes).
- DQ: `REGISTER DQ` evaluates the rule on registration (about 3 minutes here); `RUN DQ` on the weather table takes about 6 minutes; `SHOW DQ ALL INVALID` did not return within 900 s. The gateway's gate reads the single rule, `SHOW DQ INVALID RECORD coverage_ok TABLE ...`, bounded at 600 s, at onboarding and warm-up only. If DQ hangs, run the equivalent plain SQL and label the evidence "DQ-equivalent SQL".

## Objects we own (and the only ones we touch)

- Lightning databases `CW_SEC` (REST, host `data.sec.gov`), `CW_DNS` (REST, host `company-dns.mediumroast.io`), `CW_GHCN` (FILESTORE PARQUET, bucket `s3a://noaa-ghcn-pds/`); SchemaStore container `cw`.
- Views `cw.frames_<tag>_<period>`, `cw.concept_<cik10>_<tag>`, `cw.submission_<cik10>`, `cw.sic_codes`, `cw.ghcn_<year>_<element>` (station-filtered), all cached.
- USL `lightning.metastore.crosswalk.crosswalk_usl` (`sic_code`, `utility`, `station`, `weather_quarter`, `revenue_quarter`), DQ rule `coverage_ok`.
- Never DROP anything, ours or not; never GRANT, REVOKE or INVALIDATE CACHE; never touch other namespaces or databases.

## REST and filestore tables

- The `user-agent` header is the placeholder `YOUR_APP_NAME YOUR_CONTACT_EMAIL` in every committed statement and template; the runner and the gateway replace it from `CW_USER_AGENT` on the wire only. Never commit a real value and never invent a contact.
- SEC EDGAR: at most 10 requests per second (the runner and the registrar space statements that name `data.sec.gov` or `CW_SEC.*` by at least 0.1 s). Each `CREATE LIGHTNING REST TABLE` and each `CACHE TABLE` of a REST view is one request. companyconcept answers 404 for a tag a filer never used: concept tables exist per (filer, tag) and are registered on demand.
- NOAA GHCN parquet: `isS3BucketPublic "true"`, endpoint `s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com`, no credentials. The raw tables are never cached; the station-filtered views are.
- The cache is held by the driver, not the JDBC session: a driver restart drops it, and the gateway warm-up (and `scripts/warmup.py`) re-caches `CACHE_TARGETS`. A template whose objects are not cached yet returns 503 `warming`.

## Gateway contract

- The agent sends only `{template_id, params, role}` to `POST /sql/template`; it never sends SQL text. A registrar plan runs through `POST /registrar/<action>` with the plan's parameters and a signed execution contract; a registrar-kind statement sent to `/sql/template` is refused (403).
- Parameter kinds (`gateway/templates.py` PARAM_PATTERNS, mirrored in `agent/src/zetaris/client.ts`): `cik10` ten digits; `tag` one of `Revenues`, `RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax`, `RegulatedAndUnregulatedOperatingRevenue`; `period` `^CY\d{4}Q[1-3]$`; `year` `^20\d{2}$`; `quarter` 1 to 3; `station` `^US[A-Z0-9]{9}$`; `station_list` 1 to 40 station ids separated by commas; `element` TMAX or TMIN; `sic` four digits.
- Allowlist roles. Reader: `SELECT`, `SHOW`, `DESCRIBE`, `LOAD USL`, `LIST DQ`, `RUN DQ`, `SHOW DQ`. Registrar adds `CREATE LIGHTNING DATABASE CW_*`, `CREATE SCHEMASTORE CONTAINER cw`, `CREATE SCHEMASTORE VIEW ... WITH CONTAINER cw`, `CREATE LIGHTNING REST TABLE ... FROM CW_*` (one https endpoint on `data.sec.gov` or `company-dns.mediumroast.io`, no AUTH BY), `CREATE LIGHTNING FILESTORE TABLE ... FROM CW_*` (one PATH in `s3a://noaa-ghcn-pds/`, no credentials), `CACHE`/`UNCACHE TABLE` on `cw.*` and `CW_*.*`, `CREATE NAMESPACE`, `COMPILE USL ... crosswalk_usl`, `ACTIVATE USL TABLE lightning.metastore.crosswalk.*`, `REGISTER DQ`. Onboard (CLI only) adds `UPDATE USL ... DESCRIPTION`, `UPDATE DQ`, `REMOVE USL crosswalk_usl`.
- Always refused: `DROP`, `GRANT`, `REVOKE`, `INVALIDATE CACHE`, `OFFSITE*`, port 8889, two statements in one call, a trailing `;`.
- Every statement is logged to `data/evidence/sql_log.jsonl` with its sha256; replies cap at 200 rows (`row_count` holds the total).

## Scripts and verification

- SQL files live in `zetaris/sql/` as `NN_won_<name>_create.sql` / `_select.sql` pairs with the getting-started header (source, licence, format, docs, rate limit, status, caveats), declared in `zetaris/manifest.json`.
- Dry-run first (`--dry-run`), rerun with `--skip-exists`; `--timeout 600` for files that read the USL weather table.
- After creating a table, compare its row count with an independent count of the same source (the SEC response's `data` length, a pyarrow read of the same parquet files) and record both in `zetaris/README.md` with timings.
- Reference: the Zetaris getting-started repository (https://github.com/zetaris/getting-started), `docs/guides/zetaris-lightning-sql-commands.md` and `docs/guides/zetaris-lightning-sql-companion.md`.
